$${\tau _w}{{dw} \over {dt}} = a(V - {E_L}) - w$$
\end{document}.

When the current drives the potential beyound V
T the exponential term actuates a positive feedback which leads to the upswing of the action potential. The exponential is related to the quasi-instantaneous reaction of the activation variable of the sodium channel in a Hodgkin-Huxley-type neuron model. The upswing is stopped at a reset threshold which we fix at 0 mV. The downswing of the action potential, is replaced by the reset condition: \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
